FX.clear calls t.dispose() for all trails, and player.destroy also calls this.trail?.dispose() but does it remove trail from FX.trails? Player trail created via FX createTrail. Then clearWorld calls player.destroy -> trail.dispose -> then fx.clear -> trail.dispose again. Double dispose but harmless if using parent remove and geometry dispose twice (ok). But also trail might remain in fx.trails; after clear resets. Fine, but better remove from list. We can make dispose idempotent.

Fix dispose:

```js
dispose() {
  mesh.parent?.remove(mesh);
  geo.dispose(); mat.dispose();
}
```

Also in player.destroy, trail references may accumulate and double-dispose. Fine.

